===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|en|enm|talien}}, from the noun (see above). Also from {{der|en|la-med|taliare}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtæli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-tally.ogg|(US)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|tal|ly}}
* {{rhymes|en|æli|s=2}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[count]] something.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To mathematically [[calculate]] a numeric result.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[record]] something by making marks.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make things [[correspond]] or [[agree]] with each other.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1822|author=w:Alexander Pope|title=The Works of Alexander Pope|volume=9|quotee=w:Jonathon Swift|chapter=Letter IV. From Dr. Swift to Mr. Pope. August 30, 1716|others=with notes by Joseph Warton|page=11|passage=I am sorry to find they are not so well '''tallied''' to the present juncture as I could wish.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[keep score]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To correspond or agree. {{+obj|en|:with}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1957
|author=w:Karl Popper
|title=w:The Poverty of Historicism
|edition=FIRST HARPER TORCH BOOK
|chapter=24
|page=91
|text=This credulity will not be challenged here; yet it may be remarked that, assuming the unlimited and unvarying benevolence of the powerful planners, our analysis shows that it may be impossible for them ever to find out whether the results of their measures '''tally''' with their good intentions.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2019|author=Li Huang; James Lambert|title=Another Arrow for the Quiver: A New Methodology for Multilingual Researchers|journal=Journal of Multilingual and Multicultural Development|doi=10.1080/01434632.2019.1596115|page=9|text=However, one abiding weakness with such data collection is that people’s beliefs about their speech habits may not necessarily '''tally''' with reality.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} To [[check off]], as [[parcel]]s of [[freight]] going [[inboard]] or [[outboard]].

